The diffuse flux of ultrahigh-energy neutrinos ($E_{
u}\gtrsim 100\,\mathrm{PeV}$ in the abstract; $E_{
u}\gtrsim 10^{17}\,\mathrm{eV}$ in the introduction), produced by photohadronic and hadronic interactions of extragalactic UHECRs ($E_{\mathrm{CR}}\gtrsim 10^{18}\,\mathrm{eV}$), is uncertain by orders of magnitude. A KM3NeT candidate at $220^{+570}_{-110}\,\mathrm{PeV}$ contrasts with existing limits near $E_{
u}^{2}\Phi_{
u}\lesssim 10^{-8}\,\mathrm{GeV}\,\mathrm{cm}^{-2}\,\mathrm{s}^{-1}\,\mathrm{sr}^{-1}$ at $1\,\mathrm{EeV}$, which require $\gtrsim 10^{2}\,\mathrm{km}^{3}$ effective volume.
